    "voiceover_S1_HOOK": {
      "object_id": "voiceover_S1_HOOK",
      "kind": "voiceover_audio",
      "local_path": "/home/ash/ai4ia-demo-pipeline/data/generated_assets/storyline_20260624_164232_validated/audio/sections/S1_HOOK_narration_broll_voiceover.mp3",
      "filename": "S1_HOOK_narration_broll_voiceover.mp3",
      "content_type": "audio/mpeg",
      "size_bytes": 227664,
      "created_at": "2026-06-24T11:17:51.837668",
      "section_id": "S1_HOOK",
      "voiceover_text": "Across the world, conversations about artificial intelligence are raising a central question: what does it mean for technology to serve people? But because AI is expected to display so many jobs and really bring a new way of working this is an important area for us in the Caribbean to make sure that we prepare our citizens for the changing demands of the digital era. The third principle about around resiliency and sustainability ensuring that the countries in our region can adapt to the AI revolution and here again we're looking at building that capacity around things like climate change and all of the knowledge that we have in the region around natural disasters."
    },
